course: dictionary
lesson: 10787
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and value is one of them. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning to use. This is context at work. «Count each kind of coin, multiply by its value, and add all the amounts.» Here value means how much each coin is worth in money.
explain: In maths, value can mean the number a letter stands for. «Set a to 4, set b to a, change a by 1 gives a = 5 and b = 4.» When a is 4, its value is 4. When a changes to 5, its value changes too.
explain: Value can also mean how important something is. «Respect means people value and trust you.» Here value is a verb: to think someone is important and worth caring about. «Values are the beliefs a person or family thinks are important, like honesty and kindness.»
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Money, numbers and importance all fit different sentences, so read the words around value first.
fact: Value is a noun and a verb: the value of a coin, or to value a friend.
fact: Value means how much something is worth in money.
fact: The value of a digit is how much it is worth because of its place, as in place value.
fact: The value of a letter or an expression is the number it stands for, as in find the value of x.
fact: Values are beliefs that a person thinks are important, like honesty and kindness.
exercise: «Count each kind of coin, multiply by its value, and add all the amounts.» In this sentence, value means | The number of coins in the bag | How important each coin is to the shop | *How much each coin is worth in money | The colour of each coin
exercise: «In the UK people value queuing very highly.» What does value mean here? | *Think it is important | Add up the total | Sell for money | Count the people in the line
exercise: In the number 352, what is the value of the digit 5? | 3 | *50 | 500 | 5
test: «Respect means people value and trust you.» What does value mean here? | *Think you are important and worth caring about | Lose you in a crowd | Count how many you have | Sell you for money
test: Which word means the beliefs a person thinks are important, like honesty and kindness? | *Values | Expressions | Coins | Digits
exam: «Set a to 4, set b to a, change a by 1 gives a = 5 and b = 4.» What is the value of b? | 5 | *4 | 0 | 1
